      "id": "reasoning-1",
      "reason": "the cause decides which kill the case must simulate; built on the stated time-limit kill it passes at base and the control never turns red, so the section must name the uncatchable ends whose residue is what the sweep then reaps.",
      "text": "s68 says a job killed at its time limit skips the removal, but the base revision already installs `trap 'exit 143' TERM INT` under an EXIT trap that runs `rm -rvf \"$scratch\"` (reckon/crew/landing_measure.py:1270-1277, in 366cfd2166 on main since 2026-11-23T01:10Z, before the incident the section cites), so a scheduler SIGTERM at the time limit does remove the tree and only an uncatchable end (SIGKILL, OOM, node loss, or the kill grace expiring mid-removal) leaves one \u2014 which makes the first case's negative control (\"the tree is still present on the node after the limit has passed\") not red at base for a time-limit kill",
      "type": "reasoning",
      "would_change": true
    }
  ],
